#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 392pt), 109pt, 237pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 81.14pt, "The grid-like anode electrode of the PCSS produces a predominantly vertical electric field across the illuminated ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 92.66pt, "region, while fringing fields near the finger edges provide lateral components that assist in collecting carriers generated ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 104.3pt, "close to the surface. To explore the role of electrode geometry, the electrode pitch ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(410.23pt, 104.3pt, "𝑔")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(416.47pt, 104.3pt, " [Fig. 1(a)] was systematically ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 115.82pt, "varied between 20 and 80 µm. A narrow pitch enhances carrier collection through strong fringing-field overlap and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 127.34pt, "shorter lateral drift paths, whereas a wider pitch increases the optical fill factor but introduces extended low-field ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 138.86pt, "regions between fingers that limit transport efficiency. This response exhibits a strong wavelength dependence: short-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 150.38pt, "wavelength UV photons are absorbed within nanometer-scale depths, where transport is dominated by lateral drift and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 161.78pt, "surface recombination. In contrast, sub-bandgap illumination penetrates deeper into the bulk, generating carriers that ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 173.3pt, "couple to the vertical electric field. This volumetric excitation makes the photocurrent response highly sensitive to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 184.82pt, "electrode spacing, requiring an optimized pitch to balance optical access with field intensity. Importantly, the pitch ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 196.34pt, "variation does not alter the dominant")
  #line-at(222.77pt, 196.34pt, "vertical conduction path through the 450 µm substrate but instead modifies the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.86pt, "lateral access to vertical field lines, thereby shaping carrier collection dynamics, peak current, and the observed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 219.38pt, "switching speed. Systematic pitch variation, therefore, provides a controlled means of benchmarking device ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 230.78pt, "performance limits and deriving design guidelines for robust high-field switching operation. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(173.78pt, 367.13pt, "              (a) ")
  #line-at(416.23pt, 367.13pt, "     (b) ")
  #line-at(153.98pt, 376.37pt, "Fig. 1. (a) Schematic cross-section and (b) top view of the fabricated Fe-doped β-Ga")
