  #line-at(92.424pt, 494.71pt, ") for both above- and sub-bandgap excitations. The photocurrent responses exhibit distinct regimes determined ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 506.23pt, "by the carrier generation profiles, arising from the interplay between wavelength-dependent optical penetration depth ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 517.75pt, "and the electric-field distribution. For deep sub-bandgap excitation (450 and 500 nm), photocarriers are generated ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 529.15pt, "predominantly through volumetric excitation of Fe- and Ir-related deep levels within the bulk. These carriers couple ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 540.67pt, "efficiently to the vertical drift field, yielding intermediate photocurrent values (approximately 1–1.7 A at 450 nm and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 552.19pt, "< 1 A at 500 nm). Both wavelengths exhibit a clear maximum at a 40 µm pitch. This trend reflects a trade-off where ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 563.71pt, "the active collection volume expands with pitch but is eventually overtaken by the reduction in average electric-field ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 575.23pt, "intensity at larger gaps. Under above-bandgap excitation (245–255 nm), carrier generation is confined to a shallow ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 586.66pt, "near-surface region. Carrier transport is dominated by lateral diffusion and surface-driven drift, where strong surface ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 598.18pt, "recombination suppresses the photocurrent response (< 1 A). The slight increase in photocurrent observed with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 609.7pt, "increasing pitch is ascribed to the geometric expansion of the photo-active surface area, although the dominance of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 621.22pt, "diffusion-limited transport prevents significant scaling. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 637.3pt, "Near-band-edge excitation (272 and 300 nm) produces strong photocurrent response owing to an optimal penetration ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 648.82pt, "depth that simultaneously activates deep levels and maintains strong near-surface generation.  Specifically, under 272 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 660.34pt, "nm excitation at a 40 µm pitch, the photocurrent reaches a saturation plateau of ~4.14 A. This value corresponds to ")
